    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is balanced but the entry asymmetry is decisive. JPM's trend and fundamentals are clearly bullish \u2014 price above all key moving averages (10 EMA $160.50, 50 SMA $146.67, 200 SMA $136.81), +19% over 60 days, fortress balance sheet with 8.1% equity-to-assets. However, the stock is deeply overbought (RSI 81.95), momentum is decelerating (MACD histogram collapsed 87.5%), and price sits just 1.7% below the Bollinger upper band. The looming Q4 2023 earnings event in late January 2024 is a binary risk with no income statement, valuation, or sentiment data available to assess it. Chasing at $163.46 with a tight stop into an earnings event is poor risk/reward. Maintain existing positions and wait for either a pullback to the $156-160 support confluence or a confirmed breakout above $166.31 on volume before initiating new exposure.\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain existing positions; keep any new exposure modest (underweight-to-neutral) until the earnings event passes and either the pullback or breakout setup confirms.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
